{%- comment -%}
  Product card.

    {% render 'product-card', card_product: product, eager: forloop.first,
                              sizes: '(min-width: 1100px) 33vw, (min-width: 700px) 50vw, 100vw' %}

  Written against the real catalogue, which is two products:
    - the oil: 4 options, each with its own picture
    - the balm: ONE option ("9g")

  Picture. With Theme settings > Studio images on and a studio picture for
  the product's first available option, the card is a studio plate
  (.zv-studio, the warm stone every packshot in the theme stands on) with
  the maker's own packshot, cut to the product and standing on the plate's
  floor shadow (snippets/pair-offer, mode 'img', which picks the same
  packshot the pair band and the line-up show). No hover swap there: the
  other studio pictures are other options or the same product again.
  Without a studio picture: the product's own photograph, cover-cropped,
  crossfading on a fine pointer to its second photograph when there is one.

  One link per card. The whole card (picture, name, price) is the link;
  "Choose options" repeats it as a visible button for pointer users and is
  left out of the tab order and the accessibility tree, so a keyboard or
  screen reader meets each product once. Quick-add only appears where a
  single variant means there is genuinely nothing to choose; it is a real
  form, outside the link.

  The multi-buy line ("2 for $54 · 3 for $76") comes from the product's
  "Quantity offer" metafield — the same numbers the product page and the
  automatic discounts use. Those savings are fixed amounts in the shop's
  currency, so the line is only shown when the visitor sees that currency.

  heading_level exists because the correct level depends on what is above the
  card. In a grid under a section h2 the title is an h3; in a collection or
  search grid sitting directly under the page h1 it has to be an h2, or the
  document outline jumps h1 -> h3. Defaults to 3.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign p = card_product
  assign dv = p.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign media_count = p.media.size
  assign img = p.featured_media.preview_image

  assign studio = false
  if settings.studio_mode == 'on' and dv != blank
    assign dvid = dv.id | append: ''
    for n in (1..10)
      assign kv = 'studio_' | append: n | append: '_variant'
      assign ki = 'studio_' | append: n | append: '_image'
      assign sv = settings[kv] | append: '' | strip
      if sv == dvid and settings[ki] != blank
        assign studio = true
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  assign hover_img = false
  if studio == false and media_count > 1
    assign hover_img = p.media[1].preview_image
  endif

  assign sizes = sizes | default: '(min-width: 1100px) 360px, (min-width: 700px) 44vw, 88vw'
  assign loading = 'lazy'
  assign fetch = 'auto'
  if eager
    assign loading = 'eager'
    assign fetch = 'high'
  endif

  assign alt = img.alt | default: p.title | escape

  comment
    Quick-add is only honest when there is exactly one purchasable variant.
  endcomment
  assign single = false
  if p.variants.size == 1 and p.variants.first.available
    assign single = true
  endif

  assign hl = heading_level | default: 3
  if hl < 2
    assign hl = 2
  elsif hl > 6
    assign hl = 6
  endif
-%}

<article class="zcard{% unless p.available %} zcard--out{% endunless %}" data-zv-reveal>
  <a class="zcard__link" href="{{ p.url }}" aria-label="{{ p.title | escape }}">
    <div class="zcard__fig{% if studio %} zv-studio zv-studio--floor{% endif %}"{% if studio %} style="--zv-studio-pad: 13% 15% 14%"{% endif %}>
      {%- if studio -%}
        {% render 'pair-offer', mode: 'img', product: p, variant: dv,
           widths: '240,320,400,480,560,720', sizes: sizes, cls: 'zcard__img',
           loading: loading, fetchpriority: fetch %}
      {%- elsif img -%}
        <img class="zcard__img"
             src="{{ img | image_url: width: 800 }}"
             srcset="{{ img | image_url: width: 320 }} 320w,
                     {{ img | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w,
                     {{ img | image_url: width: 640 }} 640w,
                     {{ img | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w,
                     {{ img | image_url: width: 1100 }} 1100w"
             sizes="{{ sizes }}"
             width="{{ img.width }}" height="{{ img.height }}"
             alt="{{ alt }}" loading="{{ loading }}" fetchpriority="{{ fetch }}" decoding="async">
        {%- if hover_img -%}
          <img class="zcard__img zcard__img--alt"
               src="{{ hover_img | image_url: width: 800 }}"
               srcset="{{ hover_img | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w,
                       {{ hover_img | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w"
               sizes="{{ sizes }}"
               width="{{ hover_img.width }}" height="{{ hover_img.height }}"
               alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- else -%}
        <div class="zcard__blank" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- unless p.available -%}
        <span class="zcard__flag">Sold out</span>
      {%- endunless -%}
    </div>

    <div class="zcard__body">
      <h{{ hl }} class="zcard__t">{{ p.title | escape }}</h{{ hl }}>
      <p class="zcard__meta">
        <span class="zcard__price zv-num">
          {%- if p.price_varies -%}
            From {{ p.price_min | money_without_trailing_zeros }}
          {%- else -%}
            {{ p.price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
        {%- if p.compare_at_price > p.price -%}
          <s class="zcard__was zv-num"><span class="visually-hidden">Regular price </span>{{ p.compare_at_price | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</s>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if p.variants.size > 1 -%}
          <span class="zcard__opts">{{ p.variants.size }} options</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </p>
      {%- assign zoffer = p.metafields.zorev.offer.value -%}
      {%- if zoffer.breaks.size > 0 and cart.currency.iso_code == shop.currency -%}
        <p class="zcard__multi zv-num">
          {%- for t in zoffer.breaks -%}
            {%- assign ztot = p.price | times: t.qty | minus: t.save -%}
            {{ t.qty }} for {{ ztot | money_without_trailing_zeros }}{% unless forloop.last %} &middot; {% endunless %}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </a>

  {%- comment -%}
    The form sits OUTSIDE the anchor. A <button> inside an <a> is invalid
    HTML and browsers resolve the click unpredictably — you get navigation
    where you wanted an add-to-cart.

    No JS here and no second submit handler: zorev.js already binds every
    form[action*="/cart/add"], opens the drawer and refetches the cart. A
    handler of our own would POST twice and add the item twice. With JS off
    this posts normally and lands on the cart page.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if single -%}
    <form class="zcard__form" action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}" method="post">
      <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ p.variants.first.id }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">
      <button class="zv-btn zv-btn--ghost zcard__add" type="submit" data-add>
        Add to bag
      </button>
    </form>
  {%- elsif p.available -%}
    <a class="zv-btn zv-btn--ghost zcard__add" href="{{ p.url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
      Choose options
    </a>
  {%- endif -%}
</article>
